--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ABSTRACT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This sub-paper extends HCSM-14 by characterizing the orthogonal projector
P_ker onto the kernel of the winding generator H_wind = i sin(pi M / 8) on
the 14-mode multiplet at lambda = 4. We prove that the diagonal of P_ker in
the standard mode basis takes exactly two values:

    (P_ker)_ii = 2/d     = 1/2   for i in O_0
    (P_ker)_ii = (d-1)/d = 3/4   for i in O_1 union O_2

Three coefficients of the Hodge Complex Standard Model are then read as
traces of this single diagonal:

    EFT coefficient     c = (d+1) / Tr(P_ker | O_1 union O_2) = 5/9
    Mass-map coefficient  = diag(O_1 union O_2) / diag(O_0)   = (d-1)/2 = 3/2
    Kernel dimension      = Tr(P_ker)                          = 1 + (d-1)^2
                                                               = 10

The theorem is HCSM-native. The proof reduces to a single structural fact:
ker(H_wind) is invariant under the diagonal flip F but not under the full
D_4 point group. The two-value diagonal is the F-invariance of the kernel,
made explicit. Every numerical claim is verified at machine precision.

