1. INTRODUCTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1.1 Motivation
--------------

HCSM-14 establishes the winding generator H_wind = i sin(pi M / 8) on the
14-mode multiplet at lambda = 4, proves its spectrum

    {-4 sqrt(2), -2 sqrt(2), 0^(10), +2 sqrt(2), +4 sqrt(2)},

and derives the winding class partition {A, B, C} of sizes (3, 7, 4).

The present sub-paper characterizes the kernel projector P_ker of H_wind
and shows that its diagonal is the structural source of three of the
framework's leading coefficients.

1.2 Main result
---------------

Theorem 1 (Kernel-Diagonal).
Let Lambda = Z_8 x Z_8 be the HCSM substrate, let kappa_14 be the 14-mode
multiplet at lambda = 4, and let H_wind = i sin(pi M / 8). Let P_ker be
the orthogonal projector onto ker(H_wind). Then the diagonal of P_ker in
the standard mode basis takes exactly two values:

    diag(P_ker)_i = 2/d     = 1/2   for i in O_0
    diag(P_ker)_i = (d-1)/d = 3/4   for i in O_1 union O_2

1.3 Consequences
----------------

Corollary 1 (Three coefficients from one diagonal).
With P_ker as in Theorem 1:

    c = (d+1) / Tr(P_ker | O_1 union O_2) = 5/9         (EFT coefficient)

    diag(O_1 union O_2) / diag(O_0) = (d-1)/2 = 3/2     (mass-map coefficient)

    dim ker(H_wind) = Tr(P_ker) = 1 + (d-1)^2 = 10      (kernel dimension)

1.4 Relationship to HCSM-14
---------------------------

HCSM-14 proves {H_wind, P_F} = 0 (Theorem 20 there). That single algebraic
identity has a direct geometric consequence, derived here: the kernel
ker(H_wind) is F-invariant, and the diagonal of its projector is constant
on each F-cycle. The two-value diagonal and the three coefficients follow.

