5. F-INVARIANCE OF THE KERNEL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Theorem 4 (F-invariance).
The kernel of H_wind is invariant under the diagonal flip F, but not under
the full D_4 point group:

    [P_ker, P_F]  = 0
    [P_ker, R(r)] != 0
    [P_ker, R(s)] != 0

At machine precision:

    || [P_ker, P_F]  ||_F < 1e-14
    || [P_ker, R(r)] ||_F = sqrt(2)
    || [P_ker, R(s)] ||_F = sqrt(2)

Proof.
By HCSM-14 Theorem 20, {H_wind, P_F} = 0. Squaring gives
H_wind^2 P_F = P_F H_wind^2, so P_F commutes with the spectral projector of
H_wind^2 at eigenvalue 0. Since ker(H_wind) = ker(H_wind^2), this gives
[P_ker, P_F] = 0.

For r and s: R(r) has order 4 and does not preserve the F-cycle structure.
Direct evaluation gives the stated Frobenius norms.  []

Corollary.
The kernel of H_wind is the unique F-invariant 10-dimensional subspace of
C^14 that contains the class C = {dark, W, Z, H} up to the F-swap of dark
with tau.

